Z||000019||gusto||11-10-2001||03:48 AM||||Ok, can't get a loan because of my bad credit, and I haven't really driven the car much since I got it because of minor problems, that I couldn't get fixed because I can't get the car registered, because he won't give me the title, which I believe is because he never had it to begin with....whew...ok take a breath...lol. The car really wasn't in the best shape to begin with, and it certainly isn't worth $1200. He may have been thinking he could get rid of it by pawning it off on me, thinking "this kid will think I'm doing him a favor by giving him a 85 fiero for $1200" (he originally asked for $1800) He said since I was young and reminded him of himself at this age(20) he would cut me a better deal. Now there are fieros worth that much but this one isn't one of them. It's been sitting up for 3 months since he got it, he never drove or even started it every now and then. Personally I think I'm the one doing him a favor by taking the piece of s&*t of off his hands. As I said early it wasn't registered, so I couldn't drive it much, I did take it out a few times late at night(if any of you have read my other post, one of these times I took it out I got killed by my aunts mini van), and I made two trips across town to see a "friend". the last trip I made to see my "friend"..lol, I believe is when the heads cracked, so obviously this wasn't something that went wrong with the car because of the 30-40 miles I put on it. So if this old drunk(btw he really is a drunk) wants to run and tell my mom on me(he really did that to) fu**'em, he can keep his car. Ok, I'm done venting. Even though I REALLY want this car its not worth it to "ride while I pay" because I would still have to deal with him. I told him to come pick up his car Sat. and to bring my money. This car is not leaving my driveway until i get all my money back, and I don't except checks. I have admired the fiero since i was 12, I finally got 1, even though it was for only 2 months, and now in about 14hrs it'll be all over. Oh well. Sh** happens. As a small measure of pay back I'm going to, 1st collect my money and walk inside, then when he has been gone for about 10-15 mins, my brother and I are going to got out and look for him broken down on the rode...lol. Remember, cracked heads, oil as old as the car, as dirty as the car too, less than a quarter of a tank, and no plate(I live 4 blocks from a police station). Should be a good show, I'll try to remember the camera...lol. Well I guess thats all for now, my next post will be as a non-fiero owner, although technically I don't own this one, but I still drove it more then he did.    ||||reg||8
